                <pb facs="0656" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg560"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Lane reports harsh proceedings Bluefields. Martial law declared. Demands made
                    upon merchants to pay dues again. Consul summoned to give political testimony.
                    Consul at Port Limon reports Clancy refused permission to telegraph. In view of
                    this situation <hi rendition="#italic">Detroit</hi> is ordered to Bluefields to
                    watch events and report promptly, advising you and the Department by telegraph.
                    You will ask that official telegrams of consul and commander be not interfered
                    with.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
